.TH "SPEECHRECOGNITION.NOMATCH_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SpeechRecognition.nomatch_event \- SpeechRecognition: nomatch event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]nomatch\f[B]\f[R] event of the Web Speech API is fired
when the speech recognition service returns a final result with no
significant recognition.
.PP
This may involve some degree of recognition, which doesn\(cqt meet or
exceed the \f[CR]confidence\f[R] threshold.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqnomatch\(dq, (event) => { })

onnomatch = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]SpeechRecognitionEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
You can use the \f[CR]nomatch\f[R] event in an
\f[CR]addEventListener\f[R] method:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] recognition = \f[B]new\f[R] (SpeechRecognition || webkitSpeechRecognition)();

recognition.addEventListener(\(dqnomatch\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.error(\(dqSpeech not recognized\(dq);
});
.EE
.PP
Or use the \f[CR]onnomatch\f[R] event handler property:
.IP
.EX
recognition.onnomatch = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.error(\(dqSpeech not recognized\(dq);
};
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Web Speech API
